"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,625\nThe Learning Brain. Series 4: Habits\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,336\nEpisode 6\n\n3\n00:00:07,416 --> 00:00:09,552\nStress and the exam\n\n4\n00:00:12,352 --> 00:00:14,838\nYour heart races, your palms sweat,\n\n5\n00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:17,226\nand the first question looks unfamiliar.\n\n6\n00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:19,469\nExam stress is common.\n\n7\n00:00:19,786 --> 00:00:22,903\nBut two simple techniques have been tested with students.\n\n8\n00:00:23,073 --> 00:00:25,035\nWorry takes up working memory,\n\n9\n00:00:25,366 --> 00:00:28,035\nthe mental space you need to solve problems.\n\n10\n00:00:28,449 --> 00:00:35,185\nSo researchers at the University of Chicago asked students to write about their exam worries for ten minutes,\n\n11\n00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:36,962\njust before a test.\n\n12\n00:00:37,132 --> 00:00:43,041\nIn the lab, students under pressure who sat quietly scored about twelve percent lower than before.\n\n13\n00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:47,506\nThose who wrote about their worries improved by about five percent.\n\n14\n00:00:47,676 --> 00:00:49,869\nIn ninth grade biology classes,\n\n15\n00:00:50,152 --> 00:00:54,803\nanxious students who wrote about their worries scored nearly one grade point higher,\n\n16\n00:00:55,052 --> 00:00:57,597\nsay a B plus instead of a B minus.\n\n17\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,021\nStudents low in anxiety did not need it.\n\n18\n00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:02,125\nBut be careful.\n\n19\n00:01:02,511 --> 00:01:07,774\nA large replication project in 2018 did not find the effect again.\n\n20\n00:01:08,212 --> 00:01:11,079\nSo treat expressive writing as worth trying,\n\n21\n00:01:11,241 --> 00:01:12,537\nnot guaranteed.\n\n22\n00:01:12,707 --> 00:01:14,848\nThe second idea is reappraisal.\n\n23\n00:01:15,287 --> 00:01:21,950\nAt Harvard, students preparing for the GRE were told that feeling keyed up can actually help performance.\n\n24\n00:01:22,406 --> 00:01:25,767\nThey scored higher on the math section of a practice test,\n\n25\n00:01:26,035 --> 00:01:27,621\nand one to three months later,\n\n26\n00:01:27,737 --> 00:01:29,645\non the real GRE too.\n\n27\n00:01:29,815 --> 00:01:30,797\nSome caution.\n\n28\n00:01:31,205 --> 00:01:32,544\nThese studies are small,\n\n29\n00:01:32,564 --> 00:01:34,726\nand some findings have not held up.\n\n30\n00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:37,283\nAnd severe anxiety is different.\n\n31\n00:01:37,701 --> 00:01:41,139\nIt deserves real support from a counselor or doctor.\n\n32\n00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:42,206\nTry this.\n\n33\n00:01:42,598 --> 00:01:46,717\nBefore an exam, spend ten minutes writing honestly about your worries.\n\n34\n00:01:47,022 --> 00:01:48,351\nWhen your heart races,\n\n35\n00:01:48,493 --> 00:01:51,051\ntell yourself this is your body getting ready.\n\n36\n00:01:51,518 --> 00:01:53,853\nPractice under test-like conditions.\n\n37\n00:01:54,157 --> 00:01:56,587\nAnd if anxiety feels overwhelming,\n\n38\n00:01:56,647 --> 00:01:59,019\ntalk to your campus counseling service.\n\n39\n00:01:59,189 --> 00:02:00,500\nNerves are energy.\n\n40\n00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,894\nPoint them at the test.\n\n"
